# Provider brand icons — always offline in-repo

When adding or enabling a **new model provider** (or a ChatHub id that
`@lobehub/icons` does not already map), **ship the brand mark inside this
repository**. Runtime UI must not depend on a network fetch, CDN URL, or
“icons package will catch up later.”

Lesson from Xiaomi MiMo (`mimo`): ChatHub pinned `@lobehub/icons` 2.x while the
package key `xiaomimimo` only existed in v3+. Settings showed a letter fallback
until assets were vendored under `public/icons/providers/` and wired through
`ProviderBrandIcon` / `ModelBrandIcon`.

## Must

1. **Vendor the mark into the repo** before calling the provider UI done. Acceptable
   forms (any combination):
   - Static files under `public/icons/providers/<id>.*` (avatar webp/png, source SVG)
   - Inline React SVG component (required for `currentColor` / mono in dark mode)
   - Shared wrappers: `src/components/ProviderBrandIcon/`,
     `src/utils/resolveProviderIcon.ts`
2. **Wire every user-visible picker**, not only Settings sidebar:
   - Provider menu / grid / detail header
   - Model list rows
   - Chat input model trigger
   - Connection-check model selector
   - Model-select popup provider/model rows
3. **Document the source** in `public/icons/providers/README.md` (package name,
   path, license). Prefer official static packages such as
   `@lobehub/icons-static-svg` / `-png` / `-avatar` or the vendor’s own brand kit.
4. **Preserve avatar geometry** — Settings provider avatars use
   `borderRadius: 6` rounded squares; do not drop that style on fallbacks.

## Dark mode / mono

- SVG with `fill="currentColor"` **must be inline** (or a CSS mask). Loading it
  through Avatar / `<img>` freezes the fill to black and disappears on dark
  surfaces.
- Default / `type="avatar"` tiles should use an opaque avatar asset (e.g. webp),
  not the mono SVG URL.

## Do not

- Leave a letter / generic `ModelIcon` / `ProviderIcon` fallback as the shipped
  state for a first-class ChatHub provider.
- Point the UI at `https://…` icon URLs or LobeHub CDN at runtime.
- Assume bumping `@lobehub/icons` alone is enough — ChatHub may stay on an older
  major; even when the package has the logo, keep a local override until the
  installed version is confirmed and ChatHub’s provider id matches the package
  key (or is aliased in `resolveProviderIcon`).
- Map `mimo` → `xiaomimimo` (or similar) **without** checking that the **installed**
  `@lobehub/icons` version actually exports that provider.

## Checklist (new provider)

- [ ] Brand assets committed under `public/icons/providers/` (and/or inline mono).
- [ ] `resolveProviderLogoUrl` / `ProviderBrandIcon` / `ModelBrandIcon` (or
      successor) cover the ChatHub provider id and model-id prefix.
- [ ] Chat trigger + Checker + Settings list use the override (grep for bare
      `ModelIcon` / `ProviderIcon` on that id).
- [ ] Light and dark: avatar tile visible; mono inherits text color.
- [ ] README note under `public/icons/providers/`; Wiki/OpenWiki only if the
      provider page previously claimed “no logo.”

Related: **`.cursor/rules/provider-model-options.mdc`** (API/gear panels).
Implementation reference: Xiaomi MiMo path in
`src/components/ProviderBrandIcon/`, `src/utils/resolveProviderIcon.ts`,
`public/icons/providers/README.md`.
